-- Query: pt_candidates_neighbours (DR4 names)
-- Serves: Planetary-transit candidates with the neighbourhood table that links IDs between releases. In DR4 it links
--   to DR3 IDs (dr3_neighbourhood). The DR3 stand-in links to DR2 IDs (dr2_neighbourhood), which is the ID the TESS
--   Input Catalog uses. A candidate can have several rows. A candidate with no row is left out, because a LEFT JOIN
--   to these billion-row tables ran past the archive's 60 second limit: compare the number of distinct source_id
--   returned with the count.
-- Names: the draft DR4 data model of 26 Jun 2026. The schema name gaiadr4 is taken from that model's own example
--   query.
-- DR3 stand-in: dr3/pt_candidates_neighbours.adql, made from this file by make_standin.py. DR3 tables:
--   gaiadr3.dr2_neighbourhood, gaiadr3.gaia_source, gaiadr3.vari_planetary_transit.
-- Last ran without error on the DR3 stand-in: 2026-10-27 (218 rows; results/run_log.tsv).
-- Last ran on DR4: never. The archive has no DR4 until 2 Dec 2026.
-- DR4 columns this query relies on:
--   gaiadr4.dr3_neighbourhood: angular_distance, dr3_source_id, magnitude_difference, probable_match, source_id
--   gaiadr4.gaia_source: dec, phot_g_mean_mag, ra, source_id
--   gaiadr4.vari_planetary_transit: source_id, transit_depth, transit_duration, transit_period,
--   transit_reference_time
-- Lines tagged DR4ONLY have no DR3 equivalent and are dropped from the stand-in.
-- Cannot be tested before release: All of it: dr3_neighbourhood exists only in DR4. The stand-in tests the join
--   pattern with the DR3-to-DR2 table. The step from the DR3 ID to a TIC number is the job of the tic-to-gaia task.
SELECT
    pt.source_id,
    pt.transit_reference_time,
    pt.transit_period,
    pt.transit_duration,
    pt.transit_depth,
    gs.ra,
    gs.dec,
    gs.phot_g_mean_mag,
    nb.source_id AS neighbourhood_source_id,
    nb.dr3_source_id AS neighbourhood_older_source_id,
    nb.probable_match,  -- DR4ONLY
    nb.angular_distance,
    nb.magnitude_difference
FROM gaiadr4.vari_planetary_transit AS pt
LEFT OUTER JOIN gaiadr4.gaia_source AS gs
    ON gs.source_id = pt.source_id
JOIN gaiadr4.dr3_neighbourhood AS nb
    ON nb.source_id = pt.source_id
ORDER BY pt.source_id, nb.angular_distance
